    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP optimizer is heavily favoring elite speed and situational platoon advantages for today\u2019s slate. **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 83.08 score, benefiting from a soft matchup against Rocker and the high-percentage stolen base potential afforded by a slow opposing pitcher. **Mickey Moniak** (75.42) and **Josh Naylor** (75.64) round out our top-tier plays; **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime position for a breakout performance thanks to a significant 14% boost from his platoon matchup and favorable wind conditions, while **Josh Naylor** thrives against the high 4.76 xERA of McCullers Jr. Meanwhile, **James Wood** (71.32) remains a must-start out of the leadoff spot; despite a tough assignment against Lodolo, his elite xwOBA and favorable park factors make him a high-floor anchor for our scoring.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who registered a 57.00 score but fell short of the starting rotation. While the 5.06 xERA of the opposing starter provided a massive 19% efficiency boost, the heavy penalty for the same-handed platoon disadvantage ultimately pushed him behind the likes of **Tyler Soderstrom** (70.19) and **Henry Bolte** (65.40). Those two benefit significantly from the same favorable matchup but avoid the negative platoon variance that plagued **Vinnie Pasquantino**. We are also keeping a close watch on **Dalton Rushing**; his 42.77 score is suppressed by the lineup uncertainty and a negative L/L platoon split against Robbie Ray. Investors should monitor for a potential swap with **Gabriel Moreno** (55.12) if official lineups confirm **Dalton Rushing** sliding down the order. \n\nBeyond the core starters, we are tracking risk factors associated with our middle-infield pairing. **Brice Turang** (57.98) faces a stiff test against M. King, whose ability to hold runners is limiting his upside in our scarcest category, stolen bases. We\u2019ve also benched **Zach McKinstry** (39.53) and **Travis Bazzana** (31.09) as both fell below our 40-point efficiency floor due to poor park factors and SP skill matchups, respectively. We expect **Trevor Story** (64.00) to act as a stabilizer today, as the combination of park factors and wind blowing out suggests he is well-positioned to outperform his base projection despite facing a solid arm in Painter.",
